  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Discovery Engine: Feature Toggle Controls & Breaking Schema Changes",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine introduces new controls for global feature rollout stages and provides read-only access to effective feature states. However, this update includes significant breaking changes as many properties related to engine configuration, project experience, and tool display names have been made read-only.",
  "details": "Developers must update their code as several properties are now `readOnly`. This affects `delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed` and `effectiveFeatures` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine`, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngine`, and `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngine`. Similarly, `experienceState` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Project`, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaProject`, and `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaProject` is now read-only. Other fields made read-only include `toolDisplayNames` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistAnswer` and various feature toggle related fields within `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettings` schemas. Any attempts to write to these fields will now fail.\n\nYou can now precisely manage feature rollout with the new `globalFeatureToggleState` enum in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine` (and its alpha/beta counterparts), allowing states like `DELAYED`, `SCHEDULED`, `GENERAL`, and `EARLY`. The `effectiveFeatures` field provides a comprehensive, server-resolved view of all feature toggle states. Connectors gain more flexibility with `customerManagedScopes` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ActionConfig`, enabling custom OAuth scopes. Additionally, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAgent` now supports `defaultPinned` for agents, and `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DynamicTool` includes a `readonly` flag.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "breaking-change",
    "feature-management",
    "oauth",
    "connectors"
  ],
